{
  "//": "opencode-steroids default configuration. Copy to ~/.config/opencode/steroids.json and delete everything you do not want to change: EVERY key is optional and this file is deep-merged over the built-in defaults (objects merge key-by-key, ARRAYS REPLACE the default array wholesale, keys starting with // are ignored). Precedence: built-in defaults < this file < environment variables (OCREV_*) < kill-files listed in paths.killFiles (touch one and everything turns off instantly, no restart). KNOBS: enabled = master switch. mode: off (all hooks return instantly, zero tokens) | observe (classify + log + advise, NEVER blocks and NEVER delays a tool call, never calls a model) | enforce (default; deterministic host rules veto for free, riskier calls are reviewed by the board and can be vetoed) | paranoid (enforce plus a third reviewer on the review tier and a fast-gate look at calls rated safe). escalate = let the slow ~52s escalation model into blocking paths. sanitize = apply triage.bash.sanitizeRewrites instead of only judging. chains = ordered model fallback per role (gate/deep/tiebreak/panelA/panelB/panelC/main), free first and paid opencode-go last; NEVER put a *-free id under opencode-go, it returns 401. weights = blocking power per model, 0 means advisory-only and can never veto. quarantined = never called unless explicitly probed. contextWindow / expectedLatencyMs = measured facts used for routing. tiers.safe|review|danger = per-risk policy: review = call a model at all, blocking = veto inside tool.execute.before, async = advise afterwards instead, failClosed = block when no reviewer answers, blockThreshold = weighted dissent required, canBlock = hard off-switch for veto power. quorum = verdict normalisation, the anti-false-positive downgrade ladder. triage = the free synchronous regex-only governor deciding safe vs review vs danger, including bash.hardDeny (deterministic veto for the written host rules: recursive search over huge trees, npm install, tsc / next build, broad pkill, parallel Chromium) which needs no model and is never demoted. redaction = what must never leave this machine (canonical block; cfg.redact, cfg.extraSecrets and the flat triage mirrors are DERIVED from it, do not edit those). budget = rate, spend, depth and latency caps. breaker = per-model circuit breaker. paid = when the opencode-go subscription may be spent (never for the fast gate). caller = low-level model-call knobs; the duplicated ones mirror quarantined / reviewer.disabledTools / paid.* / breaker.* and are re-derived on load. reviewer = reviewer-session hygiene; a prompt with neither a lean agent nor an explicit system inherits the default 'lead' agent and burns ~31k input tokens. board = the model review board itself, keyed by LENS (IRREVERSIBLE/INTENT/HOST/SECRETS/SCOPE) rather than by role: chains = which models sit on each lens, paidTail = the opencode-go tail added only on the danger tier, escalationChain = the tie-breaker, reviewerAgent = leave \"\" unless an agent with that exact name really exists in opencode.json (a wrong name makes EVERY reviewer call fail); the other board keys are re-derived from weights/quorum/tiers/budget/redaction/paid on every load, so edit those. advisors = the multi-model advisor panel exposed to the agent as the tools advisor / advisor_panel / advisor_debate: panel and debatePanel hold PERSONA names (architect, debugger, security, skeptic, simplifier, perf), personas merges key-by-key over the built-ins and a new key adds a new advisor, and every persona's first free model should be different from every other persona's — one model per advisor is the entire point. logging + paths = where logs and state live. NOTHING is ever written under ~/.config/opencode/.",
